-- The production build of the browser application, which
-- toolchain/deploy-local.sh deploys: the same project as cabal-wasm.project,
-- which it imports so that the compiler pins, allow-newer and shared stay in
-- one place, with every package compiled at -O2, dependencies included.
--
-- It exists beside cabal-wasm.project rather than as a flag to it because a
-- change of optimisation level rebuilds everything it touches: build it with
-- `npm run build-wasm-opt`, which uses its own build directory
-- (dist-newstyle/wasm-opt), so that switching between this and the everyday
-- build in dist-newstyle/wasm never invalidates either. The first build
-- compiles every dependency again at -O2, ghc-lib-parser among them, and can
-- take over an hour; later ones only rebuild what changed.
import: cabal-wasm.project

package *
  ghc-options: -O2
